<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8">
		<title>Film Tracker - Wishlist Auto-fill</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Learn how to automatically fill in movie and series details when marking a wishlist item as watched">
		<meta name="author" content="Comp 2300">
		<!-- Bootstrap CSS Reset -->
		<link href="https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.2.1/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
	</head>
	<body>
		<!-- Navigation -->
		<nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-dark bg-dark static-top">
			<ul class="navbar-nav">
				<li class="nav-item">
					<a class="nav-link" href="/">Home</a>
				</li>
				<li class="nav-item">
					<a class="nav-link" href="/documentation">Documentation</a>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</nav>
		
		<!-- Content -->
		<div class="container">
			<h1 class="mt-4">Automatically Fill in Watched Items</h1>

			<h2 class="mt-4">Overview</h2>
			<p>
				Film Tracker makes it easier to move an item from your wishlist to your watched collection.
				When you mark a film or series as watched directly from your wishlist, the application
				automatically opens the watched-item modal and fills in the content type and title.
				This saves time and avoids entering the same information twice.
			</p>

			<h2 class="mt-4">How to Use This Feature</h2>

			<h3 class="mt-4">1. Mark an Item as Watched</h3>

			<p>
				Open your wishlist and find the film or series you have watched.
				Select the option to mark that item as watched.
			</p>

			<img
				src="/images/wishlist-mark-watched.png"
				alt="Wishlist interface showing the option to mark an item as watched"
				class="img-fluid rounded border mb-3"
			>

			<h3 class="mt-4">2. Check the Automatically Filled Information</h3>

			<p>
				The application will automatically open the modal used to add a watched film or series.
				The content type and title will already be filled in based on the item selected in your wishlist.
			</p>

			<p>
				For example, if you mark a series called <em>Breaking Bad</em> as watched,
				the modal will automatically select "Series" as the content type and fill in
				"Breaking Bad" as the title. The same behavior applies to films.
			</p>

			<img
				src="/images/watched-item-autofill.png"
				alt="Watched-item modal with the content type and title automatically filled in"
				class="img-fluid rounded border mb-3"
			>

			<h3 class="mt-4">3. Complete the Remaining Information</h3>

			<p>
				Check the automatically filled information and complete the remaining fields,
				such as the rating or any other required details.
				Once everything is ready, confirm the action to add the item to your watched collection.
			</p>

			<h3 class="mt-4">Benefits</h3>

			<ul>
				<li>No need to enter the title manually a second time.</li>
				<li>The correct content type (film or series) is selected automatically.</li>
				<li>A faster and simpler way to move items from your wishlist to your watched collection.</li>
				<li>Less risk of entering incorrect information.</li>
			</ul>

			<p class="mt-4 mb-4">
				<a href="/documentation">Back to Documentation</a>
			</p>
		</div>

		<!-- Bootstrap core JavaScript -->
		<script src="/js/jquery.min.js"></script>
		<script src="/js/bootstrap.min.js"></script>
	</body>
</html>